      "id": "seg:paragraph:overview:0004:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:overview:0004",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If your browser app uses [`WKWebView`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/WebKit/WKWebView) to display web content, [`WebKit`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/WebKit) automatically handles `WebAuthentication` challenges in webpages and requests credentials from the person using the browser.",
      "normalizedSource": "If your browser app uses [`WKWebView`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/WebKit/WKWebView) to display web content, [`WebKit`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/WebKit) automatically handles `WebAuthentication` challenges in webpages and requests credentials from the person using the browser.",
      "sourceHash": "ef47fb251988c4a8ba5462141be6698c08c740b6e13aadfdd08788ef44a937df",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Overview",
      "contextAfter": "If your browser app uses an alternative web browser engine — for example, an alternate browser engine for iPhone that you write using [`BrowserEngineKit`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/BrowserEngineKit) — when the website makes a `WebAuthentication` challenge, use [`ASAuthorizationController`](asauthorizationcontroller.md) to discover and use credentials to respond to the challenge.",
      "documentTitle": "Password use in web browsers",
      "framework": "AuthenticationServices",
      "ko": "",
